# Phase 3 — Resume Architecture Analysis

## 1. Where Resume Data Is Stored

Resume data lives in **three distinct places**, each serving a different role:

### A. In-Memory Model — [User.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/model/User.java)

The `User` POJO holds **all** resume content as flat fields:

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `name` | `String` | |
| `email` | `String` | |
| `phone` | `String` | |
| `education` | `String` | Single flat string — not structured |
| `skills` | `ArrayList<String>` | Only field that's a collection |
| `experience` | `String` | Single flat string |
| `projects` | `String` | Single flat string |
| `certifications` | `String` | Single flat string |
| `objective` | `String` | |
| `experienceYears` | `int` | Used as a boolean (0 = fresher, >0 = experienced) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `User` is an **all-fields constructor, getters-only** class with no setters. Any new data fields for templates would require modifying the constructor signature.

### B. UI Form — [ResumeBuilder.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/ResumeBuilder.java)

The `User` object is **constructed at button-click time** from 9 `JTextField`s + 1 `JCheckBox` (lines 96-112 and 169-185). The UI builds the `User` twice — once in the "Generate Resume" listener and once in the "Save to Database" listener.

### C. MySQL Database — via [UserDAO.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/dao/UserDAO.java)

`UserDAO.save(User)` persists the `User` across **7 normalized tables** in one transaction:

```
users → resumes → education → skills + resume_skills → experience → projects → certifications
```

> [!NOTE]
> The database stores **much richer structure** than the `User` model (e.g., separate `institution`, `degree`, `start_year` in education). Currently, defaults like `"Not specified"` fill the structured columns because the UI collects flat strings.

