## 3. Where Formatting / Presentation Logic Currently Exists

Formatting is **entirely inside the two `getFormattedResume()` methods**:

- [FresherResume.java:9-16](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/resume/FresherResume.java#L9-L16) — returns a plain text string
- [ExperiencedResume.java:9-17](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/resume/ExperiencedResume.java#L9-L17) — returns a plain text string

### Key Observation: Content Selection + Formatting Are Fused

Currently, a single method handles **two separate concerns**:
1. **What** to show (which fields to include) — *content selection*
2. **How** to show it (text layout, emoji prefixes, `\n` separators) — *presentation*

These two concerns are **tangled together** in the same `getFormattedResume()` method. A template system needs to separate them.

