## 4. Where PDF Generation Currently Happens

[PDFGenerator.java](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/export/PDFGenerator.java) — a single static method:

```
PDFGenerator.createPDF(String content, String fileName)
```

### What It Does
1. Creates an iText `Document`
2. Opens a `FileOutputStream` to `fileName`
3. Adds the **entire content** as **one `Paragraph`**
4. Closes the document

### What It Does NOT Do
- ❌ No fonts, no bold/italic, no heading sizes
- ❌ No sections, columns, or layout structure
- ❌ No colors, lines, or visual separation
- ❌ No template or style awareness — it's purely a string-to-PDF dumper

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The current `PDFGenerator` receives a **pre-formatted plain text `String`** from `getFormattedResume()`. It has **zero control** over layout or styling. For templates to work, PDF generation must receive **structured data** (the `User` object) instead of a flat string, so it can apply formatting itself.

### Call Chain

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["ResumeBuilder<br/>(UI button click)"] -->|"User object"| B["FresherResume /<br/>ExperiencedResume"]
    B -->|"plain text String"| C["PDFGenerator.createPDF()"]
    C -->|"writes"| D["resume.pdf"]
```

