## 5. Where Template Selection Logic Currently Exists (If Any)

### Current "Selection" — [ResumeBuilder.java:114](file:///c:/Users/shrut/Downloads/Resume%20Generator/src/com/resumegenerator/ui/ResumeBuilder.java#L114)

```java
Resume resume = isExperienced.isSelected()
    ? new ExperiencedResume(user)
    : new FresherResume(user);
```

This is a **binary toggle**, not a template system:

| Aspect | Current State |
|--------|--------------|
| Selection mechanism | `JCheckBox` ("Experienced?") |
| Number of options | 2 (hardcoded) |
| What it controls | Which **fields** to include |
| What it does NOT control | Visual style, layout, fonts, colors |
| Extensibility | Adding a 3rd type requires modifying `ResumeBuilder` |

> [!NOTE]
> There is **no template selection UI**. There is **no template abstraction**. There is **no `TemplateStrategy` interface**. The Fresher/Experienced distinction is about **data content**, not **visual design** — these are orthogonal concerns.

