## Proposed Class Responsibilities (Strategy Pattern)

### The Two Orthogonal Axes

```
                        CONTENT (what fields to show)
                     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
                     │   Fresher        Experienced     │
          ┌──────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  STYLE   │ Classic  │  Classic+Fresher  Classic+Exp    │
  (how    │ Modern   │  Modern+Fresher   Modern+Exp     │
  it      │ Minimal  │  Minimal+Fresher  Minimal+Exp    │
  looks)  └──────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
                     └──────────────────────────────────┘
```

The **"Experienced?" checkbox** controls the first axis (content).
The **new template selector** controls the second axis (style).
These are **independent** — every template should work with both Fresher and Experienced data.

### Proposed Responsibility Map

| New Concept | Responsibility | Pattern Role |
|-------------|---------------|--------------|
| `ResumeTemplate` (interface) | Defines the contract: *"Given a `User`, produce a styled PDF"* | **Strategy interface** |
| `ClassicTemplate` | Concrete strategy — traditional, serif-based layout | **Concrete strategy** |
| `ModernTemplate` | Concrete strategy — clean, sans-serif, color accents | **Concrete strategy** |
| `MinimalTemplate` | Concrete strategy — minimal, whitespace-heavy | **Concrete strategy** |
| `PDFGenerator` (refactored) | Receives a `User` + `ResumeTemplate`, delegates PDF creation to the template | **Context** |
| `ResumeBuilder` (modified) | Adds a `JComboBox` for template selection, passes the choice downstream | **Client** |

### Key Design Decision

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Who should know about Fresher vs. Experienced?**
> 
> Each template implementation decides how to handle the `experienceYears` field. If `experienceYears == 0`, the template simply omits the Experience section and emphasizes Education/Objective instead. This keeps the Fresher/Experienced logic **inside the template** rather than needing separate template subclasses for each type.
> 
> This means you do NOT need `ClassicFresherTemplate` + `ClassicExperiencedTemplate`. You need just `ClassicTemplate` — and it internally checks `user.getExperienceYears()`.
